DATABASE MIGRATIONS

This project uses Alembic (SQLAlchemy’s migration tool) to manage database
schema changes over time.

Alembic is the source of truth for schema evolution.
All migration files are stored in the /migrations/versions directory.

The application database is named: priceorbit_db


PREREQUISITES

- MySQL installed and running locally
- Python virtual environment activated
- Environment variables configured


FIRST-TIME DATABASE SETUP

To initialize the database schema on a clean database using Alembic:

alembic upgrade head

This command will:
- create all database tables
- create the alembic_version table
- bring the database to the latest schema version


MAKING SCHEMA CHANGES

After modifying SQLAlchemy models, generate a new migration:

alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe schema change"

Apply the migration:

alembic upgrade head

All schema changes after initial setup must be handled using Alembic migrations.


ROLLING BACK MIGRATIONS

To roll back the most recent migration:

alembic downgrade -1

To roll back all migrations:

alembic downgrade base


DEVELOPMENT DATABASE RESET (DESTRUCTIVE)

For local development and testing only, a full database reset script is provided:

python migrations/init_db.py

This script:
- drops all existing tables
- recreates tables directly from SQLAlchemy models
- bypasses Alembic migrations

After running this script, synchronize Alembic’s migration state:

alembic stamp head

DO NOT use this script in production environments.


NOTES

- Alembic should be used for all schema changes after initial setup.
- init_db.py exists only for local development resets.
- The database should not be modified manually during normal application runtime.
